        "The fastest verification is the one you never touch. When your customer pays, your mobile-money operator already sends you a confirmation message on the spot. That text is the most reliable proof a payment happened, because it comes from the telco itself, and yet most merchants let it sit unread while they squint at a customer's screenshot instead. The KODA Sentinel app turns that operator message into an instant, structured verdict without a single tap from you.",
        "Setup is a one-time affair. You install Sentinel on the Android phone that holds your mobile-money SIM, pair it once with your {{brand}} account, and from then on every incoming operator confirmation is read and forwarded securely for matching. When a forwarded message lines up with an open order, that order confirms itself and fires a webhook so your systems react automatically, exactly as described in {{post:payment-verified-webhooks}}. This is the automatic path, Door 3 among the {{post:five-doors-verify-mobile-money}}, and it feeds the very same engine as every other door.",
        "Step by step, the flow is simple. Your customer pays and quotes their reference. Your operator, be it M-Pesa, Orange Money, Airtel Money or MTN MoMo, texts your phone. Sentinel detects that the message is a payment confirmation from a known operator, forwards it, and {{brand}} matches the reference against the open order, applies its fraud checks, and returns a verdict in about three seconds. The order flips to verified on its own. Nobody typed a code, nobody compared a screenshot, and the customer is served faster than a manual check could ever manage.",
        "A natural worry is privacy, and it is worth being precise. Sentinel does not vacuum up your inbox. It only forwards payment confirmations from known operators; ordinary personal messages are ignored and never leave the phone. The app also keeps a heartbeat so you can always see it is alive and connected on your dashboard, and if the phone briefly loses signal, any confirmations that arrived while it was offline are queued on the device and back-filled the moment it reconnects. Nothing is silently dropped.",
        "Why does this matter so much for African merchants? Because the alternative is a person, and people get busy. During a rush, the cashier who is meant to check each payment starts waving customers through on a glance at a screenshot, which is exactly the gap fraudsters wait for. Automation removes the human bottleneck at the worst possible moment. The busier you get, the more valuable hands-free verification becomes, because the machine does not tire, look away, or feel pressured by a queue.",
        "The common mistake is assuming that automatic means unchecked. It does not. Every message Sentinel forwards still passes the full anti-forgery test described in {{post:balance-chain-fake-sms}} before it is allowed to verify anything, along with the fraud scoring that guards all five doors. Auto-verification is faster than a manual check and stricter than a human eyeball, not a shortcut that trades safety for speed. A forged or replayed message is rejected just as firmly whether a person or the app submitted it.",
        "Because Sentinel simply reads the operator's own notification on your own phone, it needs no telco API, no special contract and no integration to begin, which is what lets any merchant start today with the hardware already in their pocket. There is no waiting on a partnership team, no minimum volume, and no bank in the loop. It also composes cleanly with the other doors: you can run Sentinel for the bulk of automatic confirmations while still keeping the Manual Console, WhatsApp or USSD available for the odd exception or a staff member working from a different phone. Developers who want to build on the events it produces can start from {{page:developers}}.",
        "Hands-free, fraud-checked payment confirmation on the phone you already own, with no new hardware and nothing to integrate. That is the whole promise. {{page:getstarted}} with {{brand}}, install Sentinel on your mobile-money handset, and let your payments start verifying themselves while you get back to serving customers.",
